    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287">

                <pb facs="0342" n="282" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg282"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Eustis</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-09-04"><hi rendition="#italic">September 4,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 516.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 358,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d287-f1"/> of the 23d ultimo, inclosing a
                    copy of a letter from Mrs. Waller to her <pb facs="0343" n="283" xml:id="pg283"
                    /> husband, the original of which was forwarded to Mr. Waller by you through the
                    foreign office.</p>
                <p>The Department would be glad to be informed as to whether Mr. Waller’s letters
                    have been promptly delivered to him.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
